    "narrative": "For June 28, 2026, **Max Muncy** headlines our lineup with a 66.40 efficiency score, capitalizing on a soft matchup against Aldegheri (5.54 xERA). The platoon advantage provides a 7% boost, and the significant SP skill delta (+19%) makes him our primary anchor in a day where most of our core faces high-tier arms. **James Wood** also presents an elite upside at 62.72; while he faces a tougher arm in Bradish, the 16% park factor uplift and his role atop the order solidify his position. Despite his high stolen base potential, he is tempered by an elite hold pitcher, but his xwOBA remains a reliable indicator for production.\n\n**Brice Turang** and **Josh Naylor** round out our 60+ tier, both benefiting from favorable lineup positioning. We are closely monitoring **Corbin Carroll**, whose 56.80 score is depressed by a 14% penalty due to the SP skill of Rasmussen; however, his unique ability to impact the SB category keeps him as a must-start even when efficiency metrics are squeezed by pitching quality. **Seiya Suzuki** and **Jose Caballero** are our riskiest starts today, hovering near the 40-point floor. **Jose Caballero** in particular is battling a 13% platoon penalty and a bottom-of-the-order assignment, making his presence in the lineup purely a play for his elite sprint speed contributions.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Alex Freeland**, who posted a 46.41 score\u2014landing just above the threshold for marginal starts but failing to unseat our primary infielders. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, his #8 lineup slot creates a significant projected efficiency drag compared to the top-of-order opportunities afforded to **Travis Bazzana**. We continue to keep **Mickey Moniak** glued to the bench due to his platoon disadvantage against Prielipp, ensuring we preserve our limited game caps for hitters with better situational alignments. Keep a close eye on the weather and official confirmations for **Austin Riley**, as his matchup against Ray carries risk if the wind shifts or lineup configurations change.",
